Z||000003||theogre||08-28-2000||10:45 AM||||I've got a bunch of stuff on the DIS version of the motor in my cave. Not so much for the distributor version. (Link on bottom of this page.)<P>In short the 2.5 is about the last of the Cast Iron 4 cyls. All the others GM is using that I know of are aluminum. There's 2 versions of the duke used in Fiero, and not much is interchangable between them. We tell them apart here by either distributor or DIS ignition. (Or by year. DIS started in 87)<P>You question is kind of vague. Advantages etc compaired to what? Each motor out there has its own set of issues.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 08-28-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||moonie||08-28-2000||08:48 PM||||theogre , <P>i am kinda new to fiero's & i had saw others post about " Iron Dukes "<P>i was just looking for knowledge , like are they a better engine than a non-duke ?<BR>( lol ) <BR>or do they have inherent built in problems , oil leaks , overheating , etc. etc. <P>also , i am wondering do i have one.<BR>i have a 85 se 4cyl. the head is cast iron i know , its off now , i think the block is cast iron also , but was looking for more validation.<P>thanks again <BR>Moonie <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||theogre||08-28-2000||10:56 PM||||yeah you probly have one. the pictures on the homestead site should give you a better idea.<P>Not really any more problem with them than any other engine GM ever made. Less actually than some.<P>At this age any motor is likely to leak oil or coolant.<P>When you put the head back on REPLACE ALL the head bolts. ALL of them. The original ones are known to be weak. This is the only kind of major defect I know of that affects all years. The rest are all minor and should have been fixed if/when the recall work was done. (The bad batch of piston rods was only an 84 problem that I can tell)<P>Replace the exhaust manifold bolts as well if they are beat looking. the rest of the bolts for brackets, intake, etc, are fine to reuse.<P>Even if the recall work wasn't done you are fixing one of it's major components..... the valve cover gasket. The replacement of the head bolts will fix the other. (The bolts are known to break and result in coolant/oil leaking on the exhaust.) The rest of the recall was mainly making sure all the wires are protected from the exhaust heat.||||reg||1
